# Secret-scan allowlist — S49 security campaign.
#
# Format: <file-path-regex>|<pattern-name-regex>
#   a line matches (suppresses its finding) when BOTH regexes match
#   (bash =~, ERE syntax). Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# IMPORTANT: entries here must be publicly-known, non-secret constants that
# were independently verified during the S49 audit
# (docs/security/SECURITY_AUDIT.md). Never use this file to silence a real
# credential.

# Google's own PUBLIC devsite/browser API keys embedded in the HTML of
# source.android.com / developers.google.com pages; captured verbatim inside
# the android_bytecode_doc.json research snapshot (working tree + the copy
# shipped inside the legacy v0.0.1-Brahma release asset). These keys are
# published by Google in public HTML — public-by-design, not credentials.
.*android_bytecode_doc\.json|GOOGLE_API_KEY

# The F-Droid index changelog text describing "basic auth using urls" with a
# literal placeholder (user:password@linx-server.example).
.*fdroid_index_v2\.json|URL_EMBEDDED_CREDENTIAL
